==German==
{{wikipedia|Mohammed (Name)|lang=de}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|de|Muhammad}} {{i|see usage notes below}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{etyl|ar|de}} {{m|ar|مُحَمَّد}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmoː.(h)a.mɛt/|lang=de}} {{i|normal}}
* {{audio|De-Mohammed.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
:* {{IPA|/moˈha.mɛt/|lang=de}} {{i|less common}}
:* {{IPA|/ˈmɔɐ̯.mɛt/|lang=de}} {{i|sometimes in casual speech}}

===Proper noun===
{{head|de|proper noun|g=m}}

# [[Muhammad]] {{gloss|the prophet of Islam}}
# {{given name|male|from=Arabic|lang=de}} ''very popular among'' {{m|en|Muslim|Muslims}}

====Usage notes====
* The spelling ''Mohammed'' remains the common one in German, at least when referring to the founder of Islam. The spelling {{m|de|Muhammad}} is chiefly restricted to scientific and inner-Islamic usage.

